an-leaning states in presidential politics, having backed the GOP by wide margins in recent cycles. With the incumbent term-limited, the seat is open, removing any incumbency cushion, but the state's R+15 lean remains the dominant force. No public polls of the race or expert ratings exist yet, so the forecast rests on partisan fundamentals.\n\nThe main wildcard is Gov. Andy Beshear, a Democrat whose popularity at home and national campaign travels have fueled 2028 speculation. A home-state nominee could trim the Republican edge somewhat, but even popular statewide Democrats have not come close in Kentucky's presidential contests. With no market pricing or ratings to weigh, the Republican-favored outlook stands on the state's durable lean.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0468, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1024, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.09, "margin": -15.0}]}